// G3 grammar fixture for docs/prds/v0_6/angle-units-surface-convergence.md cluster C
// (ratified decision 7a: accept U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT as a unit-multiply operator).
//
// grammar_confirmed: true — leaf κ (task #5784, "Scanner accepts U+00B7 as
// unit-multiply") LANDED the acceptance. This fixture now parses AND compiles
// clean: `tree-sitter parse --quiet` exits 0, and `reify eval` prints all three
// bindings. The external token `UNIT_MUL_OP` fires on ASCII `*` OR U+00B7, both
// gated identically by `is_unit_start` (tree-sitter-reify/src/scanner.c), and
// `lower_unit_expr` maps both spellings to the same `UnitExpr::Mul`, so each
// binding below evaluates identically to its `*`-spelled twin.
//
// (Historical: this fixture was committed RED, failing with a 3-byte ERROR node
// over the `·` on each `let` line, because U+00B7 appeared nowhere in the
// grammar or scanner.)
//
// CONSUMED BY crates/reify-compiler/tests/harness_units/unit_middot_mul_tests.rs,
// which reads this file from disk and asserts (i) zero Error diagnostics and
// (ii) all three value cells PRESENT — the anti-silent-drop lock — each with a
// (si_value, dimension) equal to its `*`-spelled twin's. Because a tracked `.rs`
// names this fixture, it is ALSO listed in scripts/verify.sh's
// `_RUST_COUPLED_RI_FIXTURES`; test_verify_scope.sh's PG-DRIFT scenario derives
// that set by grepping tracked `.rs` files and goes RED if the two drift apart.
// Editing a `let` line below therefore changes a test input — don't. That is
// ENFORCED, not merely asserted, on three axes: assertion (ii) pins each binding
// against a `*`-spelled twin string held in the test AND pins the cell COUNT at 3
// (so a fourth `let` cannot be silently ignored by a test that iterates its own
// table), and `compile_fixture` pins the U+00B7 SPELLING of each `let` line below
// — per line, against the `·` count implied by that binding's twin, so a comment
// anywhere in this header (`//` or `/* … */`) can neither break the check nor
// stand in for a `let` line that lost its `·`. That last lock exists because `·`
// and `*` lower to the SAME `UnitExpr::Mul`, which makes a `sed 's/·/*/g'` over
// this file invisible to every value assertion — the one edit that would gut the
// fixture.
//
// Why it matters: `Display for DimensionVector` (reify-core/src/dimension.rs)
// joins base-unit parts with U+00B7, so `reify eval` prints lines like
// `7850 kg·m^-3` and `5 m^2·kg·s^-2·rad^-1`. κ makes the UNIT SUBSTRING of such a
// line readable: `7850kg·m^-3` now parses and evaluates identically to its
// `*`-spelled twin `7850kg*m^-3`.
//
// STILL OPEN — κ closed the READ direction for the MIDDLE DOT only; the full
// `reify eval` line is NOT round-trippable yet. The SPACE between magnitude and
// unit is a second, independent blocker κ did not touch. Measured on this branch
// with ./target/debug/reify eval:
//     let a = 7850 kg·m^-3   → exit 1, `Parse error: invalid let: …`
//     let a = 7850 kg*m^-3   → exit 1, the SAME error — so the space is
//                              pre-existing, not a `·` regression
//     let a = 7850kg·m^-3    → exit 0, prints `S.a = 7850 kg·m^-3`
// Normalizing what the curated labels EMIT is leaf λ; the `·` round-trip property
// test is leaf μ (#5789), which must NOT assume the space is already handled.
// `Display` is deliberately unchanged here.

structure def UnitMiddotMul {
    let torque_like = 5N·m
    let with_div    = 5N·m/rad
    let composed    = 5m^2·kg·s^-2
}
